Load LIBERO's initial-state files with weights_only=False.

torch 2.6 flipped the default of `torch.load(weights_only=...)` from False to True. The benchmark's
init_files/*.pruned_init pickle numpy arrays, so on this repo's torch 2.8 every eval dies at the
first task with:

    _pickle.UnpicklingError: Weights only load failed.
    WeightsUnpickler error: Unsupported global: GLOBAL numpy.core.multiarray._reconstruct

These files ship inside the LIBERO repo itself and are the benchmark definition, not downloaded
artifacts, so loading them unrestricted is safe.

Only the path LIBERO exposes to external evaluators (benchmark/__init__.py) is patched; the
libero.lifelong training framework has the same issue but is unused here.

diff --git a/libero/libero/benchmark/__init__.py b/libero/libero/benchmark/__init__.py
index 2b833d0..47451a0 100644
--- a/libero/libero/benchmark/__init__.py
+++ b/libero/libero/benchmark/__init__.py
@@ -161,7 +161,10 @@ class Benchmark(abc.ABC):
             self.tasks[i].problem_folder,
             self.tasks[i].init_states_file,
         )
-        init_states = torch.load(init_states_path)
+        # v4world: torch>=2.6 defaults to weights_only=True, which refuses these files because
+        # they pickle numpy arrays (numpy.core.multiarray._reconstruct). They are the benchmark's
+        # own init_files/*.pruned_init shipped in this repo, so loading them fully is safe.
+        init_states = torch.load(init_states_path, weights_only=False)
         return init_states
 
     def set_task_embs(self, task_embs):
